{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/470625-best-way-to-toughen-up-a-character","id":470625,"title":"Best way to toughen up a character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-06T19:36:44-07:00","id":470625,"title":"Best way to toughen up a character?","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I'm trying to figure out the best way to toughen up my hunter character (pre-GMC) so as to be able to take/avoid a hit. Raising attributes is really expensive, so I'm looking at merits and such that I can use. What's the cheapest way I can either raise my health or raise my defense/armor?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Character: </span></span><a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=983092\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...sheetid=983092</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Assume I already have a bulletproof vest in my possession, and don't want to wear any more obvious armor</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T04:25:53-07:00","id":471087,"title":"","content":"Well, its kind of a technicality, and I feel like your storyteller would be entirely justified in saying these two dont stack, but technically, the 1/1 armor boost from Boxing and the 1/1 armor boost from Berserker are named two different things and since the general rule is &quot;Two things with different names stack, so long as it makes sense&quot;, these two will stack for an effective 2/2 armor against bashing applicable even if you're naked. I think the one from Bersker even works against Lethal, but I'm not sure. Cant quite remember.<br /> Other than that, if you're willing to invest into it, Fencing/Kendo will let you do a Repost, which is essentially a dodge action, and if anyone attacks you, you get an attack off against him. So dodging and attacking simultaneously, essentially.<br /> <br /> Although to be fair, I always feel like this kind of &quot;maximising your characters damage/dodge/fight/whatever&quot; is alittle anathema to how the World of Darkness is suposed to work. If theres that much violence in your games, your character is probably better off investing into some heavy duty firearms, explosives and a discount agreement with the local hospital. Going toe-to-toe with anything supernatural as a hunter is a good way to get yourself murder-faced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T08:25:58-07:00","id":471229,"title":"","content":"The Giant merit would give you an extra health box. Various fighting styles can give you bonuses to Defense but they tend to be more about Brawl or Weaponry. Joining a conspiracy could go a long way towards getting you a benefit of some sort to survival. Your character looks pretty tough as is, to be honest. If you're of the mind that the best defense is a good offense, you might grab Gunslinger.<br /> <br /> The My Brother's Keeper tactic might serve you well, potentially giving you Defense bonuses in accordance with the primary actor's successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T12:18:51-07:00","id":471433,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if conspiracies actually exist in this game - if they do our characters certainly don't know about them at this point.<br /> <br /> I'm liking berserker, though the roll to not attack friends worries me a bit. Though I suppose it fits with wolfblooded well. It does provide defense against lethal. Maybe combat marksmanship to boost initiative (though the fifth dot of that is a bit cheesy for me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T18:54:48-07:00","id":471956,"title":"","content":"Then don't go to the fifth dot then! It's all about what kind of character you want to play. If you have a potential Conspiracy in mind, then all remember to make your character look like an attractive recruit. If that doesn't sound appealing then maybe this character shouldn't join the possibly non-existing splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:57:22-07:00","id":474736,"title":"","content":"We were discussing Ascending Ones OOC, as being a good fit for our group. My character already deals drugs for organized crime, and we have an egyptian archeologist in the mix as well.<br /> <br /> My character's meant to mostly be a thug. Tough, hard to hit, and good at making herself look like someone you don't want to mess with. Or alternately the person you want to go after first while the rest of the party sets something up (we're working on a tactic for that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T08:31:29-07:00","id":476994,"title":"","content":"In Mirrors there are rules for buying extra health, the ST might say no but you could always try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}